  "limitations": [
    "vTaskDelay executes in an emulator over authored kernel state, reusing vTaskSuspendAll, prvAddCurrentTaskToDelayedList, vListInsert, the list primitives and the whole of xTaskResumeAll as guarded original code. No hardware timer or interrupt is delivered.",
    "configASSERT, the critical-section diagnostic body and vPortYield are supplied stubs; vPortYield is a no-op return, so the context switch it would trigger is not modeled. The routine completes and the pending switch is visible only in the kernel state it leaves (the task moved off the ready lists onto a delayed list).",
    "The delayed/overflow/suspended list contents are authored. Indefinite blocking (ticks == 0xffffffff) is reachable only from other callers and is modeled but not exercised here; live preemption and the timer frequency remain unproved."
  ],
